"texte": [
"Ladies and gentlemen, esteemed delegates, we gather today at a critical juncture in human history. Over the past few decades, hyper-consumption has been relentlessly promoted as the ultimate pathway to personal happiness and economic prosperity. We have been conditioned to buy items we scarcely need, with money we often do not have, to impress people we barely know. However, this insatiable appetite for material accumulation has exacted a devastating toll on both our planet and our psychological well-being.",
"Consider, first, the environmental catastrophe unfolding before our eyes. Every garment discarded after a single season and every electronic device rendered obsolete within two years contributes to mountains of toxic waste and depletes finite natural resources. Although corporations frequently employ 'greenwashing' tactics to soothe our collective conscience, the stark reality remains unchanged: infinite economic growth on a finite planet is a mathematical impossibility.",
"Moreover, excessive consumption subtly enslaves us in our daily lives. In order to sustain an ever-expanding lifestyle, individuals are forced to work longer hours, sacrificing leisure, family time, and personal passions. Consequently, our homes become cluttered with possessions that demand constant maintenance, insurance, and storage, transforming what we own into burdens that own us.",
